<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/004ea0c68c4f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Monday, Scarlett Johansson threatened legal action against OpenAI for allegedly copying and imitating her voice after she refused to license it to the company." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7432" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0103d6a9e818> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Jeffrey Bennett, the Sag-Aftra general counsel, says: \"I am willing to bet there are quite a few companies out there that don't even understand that there are rights in voice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3695" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/042652050b96> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The company provided The Washington Post with documents and recordings clearly meant to support OpenAI CEO Sam Altman's defense against Johansson's claims." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3698" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0d205fc1ffa1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Saturday Night Live highlighted the Johansson similarity during its Season 49 finale Saturday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3697" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/110922d7e089> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "who voiced an artificial-intelligence assistant in the 2013 sci-fi romance \"Her.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3664" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/11559f27ae01> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ChatGPT has released a new voice assistant feature inspired by Scarlett Johansson's A.I. character in *Her*." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3697" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/14d13682e4c8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The retreat by OpenAI follows a backlash to the artificial voice, known as Sky, which critics described as being overly familiar with users." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3665" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/166ab845d8cd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Visar Berisha, an Arizona State University professor who studies AI speech technology, said it is hard to predict how advanced AI voice assistants that speak with human-like personalities will change society." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3696" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1b36e0817aa6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "General counsel for the SAG-AFTRA performers union, Jeffrey Bennett, told Reuters that he hopes Johansson's feud with OpenAI motivates lawmakers to create \"a federal right for voice and likeness similar to the federal protections for a copyright.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3698" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2382d0be9fbf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It also revealed it was developing a tool called Media Manager that would allow creators and content owners to flag their work and whether they wanted it included in training of AI models, which \"learn\" from a mass of material taken from the internet." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3695" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/239806f075dc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The new model, known as GPT-4o, transforms the chatbot into a voice assistant that can interpret facial expressions, detect emotion and even sing on command." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3696" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/28f3769eebc2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson Says She Was ‘Shocked, Angered and in Disbelief’ After Hearing ChatGPT Voice That Sounds Like Her — Read Statement" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3697" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/34bf8d35505d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a time when we are all grappling with deepfakes and the protection of our own likeness, our own work, our own identities, I believe these are questions that deserve absolute clarity." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7434" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/39d32fd77d99> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Sky” may also have implicated the rights of Annapurna, which produced Her, if Altman was looking to replicate Johansson’s performance in the film." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7432" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3f1b63e94d70> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson has said she was left \"shocked\" and \"angered\" after OpenAI launched a chatbot with an \"eerily similar\" voice to her own." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5852" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3f33802d766c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI has spent months making the rounds with studios and producers showcasing its Sora text-to-video tool and discussing potential licensing deals, according to people familiar with the meetings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3671" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/43430bc0a2fe> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sky was 1 of 5 voices OpenAI unveiled in September when it added an audio conversation mode to its ChatGPT chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3663" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/481f80ccea08> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Altman didn't give up. In mid-May, he texted Lourd, co-chairman of Creative Artists Agency, asking if Johansson might reconsider---he wanted to show the actress something he'd been working on, people familiar with the interaction said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3671" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/50d9a8792625> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI President Greg Brockman responded in a longer post on Saturday, which was signed with both his name and Altman's, laying out the company's approach to long-term AI safety." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3665" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/510a76404e9f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In a September interview, The Post asked Peter Deng, OpenAI's vice president of consumer products, whether the voice was meant to resemble the actress's." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3663" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/52c3e1537320> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sky, like Samantha, possesses a voice that sounds far more human than the robotic staccato of Siri or Amazon's Alexa." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3668" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/52cce857c72e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson 'shocked' by AI chatbot imitation" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5852" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5441c0f29c0a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Johansson, in a statement provided to Variety, said her lawyers contacted OpenAI to have the voice of Sky, one of the new voices in the GPT-4o chatbot, pulled down." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7434" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/55d3483a32d4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Behind the Scenes of Scarlett Johansson’s Battle With OpenAI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3671" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5fab9c1e2cc2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Days before OpenAI demonstrated its new, flirty voice assistant last week, the actress Scarlett Johansson said, Sam Altman, the company's chief executive, called her agent and asked that she consider licensing her voice for a virtual assistant." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3659" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/67f524113bf6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson says she is 'shocked, angered' over new ChatGPT voice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3696" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/691f8eb3e97e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson Rebukes OpenAI Over ‘Eerily Similar’ ChatGPT Voice" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3664" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6a581eb1b99a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "9 months later, my friends, family and the general public all noted how much the newest system named 'Sky' sounded like me." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3660" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e587c4809b2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ChatGPT suspends Scarlett Johansson-like voice as actor speaks out against OpenAI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5851" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7348c086a0c4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sky voice actor says nobody ever compared her to ScarJo before OpenAI drama" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3698" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/73601ae28aca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson says OpenAI copied ‘Her’ voice after she said no" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3663" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/83148e7fd159> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI said it is hitting the pause button on the update after comparisons with a fictional voice assistant portrayed in the quasi-dystopian film \"Her\" by Johansson." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3665" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/85c4a0bb9e2c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "generate essays" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3663" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/88b9e7553237> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Mark Chen, a company research lead, told the assistant that he was nervous to be doing a live demo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3659" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8d0fba1a2d31> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI is pausing the use of a voice named Sky that is part of a new demo of ChatGPT 4.0's Voice Mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3697" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8f92faccc87f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "News Corp, owner of The Wall Street Journal, struck a content-licensing partnership with OpenAI Wednesday that could be worth more than $250 million over five years." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3671" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/90c4254cec28> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Altman and his fellow co-founder Greg Brockman defended the company over the weekend, stating that it would not release a product if there were safety concerns." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5851" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/91e0164873d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Paul Skye Lehrman, who has over a decade of experience as a voiceover artist and is suing an AI startup, said he’s gotten roughly 50 percent less work since last year." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7432" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9275278ac8cf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The company pulled back its Sky voice days after several top members of its safety team resigned, with a key researcher, Jan Leike, saying after he quit that the company was prioritizing “shiny products” over safety culture and processes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5851" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/92cda4b64ab4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On Monday, the lead counsel for the New York Times’ own suit against OpenAI sent a letter to the presiding judge, accusing the company of delaying a similar discovery process by “taking weeks to respond, dragging out negotiations over a protective order, and refusing to quickly produce basic information.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5854" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/994573e6e2b9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson’s Statement About Her Interactions With Sam Altman" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3660" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9c6d593d47f4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "I am willing to bet there are quite a few companies out there that don't even understand that there are rights in voice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3695" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9ec574511d6f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Johansson---who just three years ago waged a blistering and public legal campaign against Disney---hired a legal team to demand answers from Altman and OpenAI and issued an excoriating statement." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3671" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9fc829081ac3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Actress Scarlett Johansson is threatening legal action against OpenAI, alleging the artificial intelligence start-up copied her voice after she refused to license it to the company." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3663" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a27637fce296> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson issued a statement alleging that the artificial intelligence start-up OpenAI copied her voice for an audio conversation function added to its popular ChatGPT chatbot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3668" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a3e59fee70a0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Exactly how stupid was what OpenAI did to Scarlett Johansson?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3662" .

