    airo:evidenceText "released in September that allows users to talk to its AI tool instead of type and hear responses in five different voices." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3664" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aa83850e05e5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson lawyers up over ChatGPT voice that ‘shocked and angered’ her" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3665" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ac7111e448dc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sag-Aftra, the US actors' union, feels this is a teachable moment for the tech industry." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3695" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/afe868ca7ebb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It makes sense that SAG-AFTRA publicly praised Johansson’s stance here against OpenAI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5854" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b31702659cd2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson's powerful Hollywood agent, Bryan Lourd, wanted answers when he made an urgent call to Sam Altman last week: What do you think you're doing?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3671" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b3952fadcbd1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI executives have repeatedly declined to answer questions on whether its text-to-video tool Sora was trained on YouTube videos." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7432" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bb1b5c28dac9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When Apple first launched Siri, per Guzman, \"it was very much a conversation between a male executive and a female assistant.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3668" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c0a7c2150bab> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson’s OpenAI clash is just the start of legal wrangles over artificial intelligence" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3695" .

