<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ea385be61955> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI, the research firm whose 2022 launch of ChatGPT single-handedly pushed “artificial intelligence” into the mainstream, isn’t often inclined to back down from the knotty disputes...",
        "OpenAI, the research firm whose 2022 launch of ChatGPT single-handedly pushed “artificial intelligence” into the mainstream..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5854" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ed483ffb5f4a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Scarlett Johansson-OpenAI dispute is straight out of ‘Her’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3668" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eeffda6a277b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In an interview after the event, Mira Murati, OpenAI's chief technology officer, told The Verge that the similarities to Ms. Johansson's voice were incidental." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3659" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f16f836ebd18> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 of Johansson's signature roles was as the voice of a futuristic version of Siri in the 2013 film Her and, for the actor, the similarity was stark." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3695" .

