<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/AISystem/ef6083019639> a airo:AISystem ;
    rdfs:label "Her" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.9"^^xsd:float ;
    airo:extractionMode "explicit" ;
    airo:hasDescription "Her" ;
    airo:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c4c22cb6230c> ;
    airo:hasSourceDocument <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/document/3662> .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/243be730ca1a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Scarlett Johansson's powerful Hollywood agent, Bryan Lourd, wanted answers when he made an urgent call to Sam Altman last week: What do you think you're doing?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3671" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8749dea7d73a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last September, I received an offer from Sam Altman, who wanted to hire me to voice the current ChatGPT 4.0 system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3660" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aa6a6692a9fa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "And in September, authors George RR Martin and John Grisham also announced a plan to pursue a claim, over allegations their copyright had been infringed to train the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5852" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c4c22cb6230c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The same day, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman posted on X a one-word reference to the 2013 movie \"Her,\" in which Johansson was the voice of an emotional companion AI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3662" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c92bfe3ae7dc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A day after OpenAI's announcement, Google held its annual developer conference where it unveiled its own personal AI assistant, also voiced by a female, known as Project Astra." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3696" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/155d29111112> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 days before the ChatGPT 4.0 demo was released, Mr. Altman contacted my agent, asking me to reconsider. Before we could connect, the system was out there. As a result of their actions, I was forced to hire legal counsel, who wrote two letters to Mr. Altman and OpenAI, setting out what they had done and asking them to detail the exact process by which they created the 'Sky' voice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3660" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dcfde8731088> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Here is Scarlett Johansson's statement on Monday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3660" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/754f03a8d05a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The new model, known as GPT-4o, transforms the chatbot into a voice assistant that can interpret facial expressions, detect emotion and even sing on command." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3696" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0dc2e4438c96> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI offered in September to hire the actress to voice its chatbot, according to her version of events." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3662" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fd1c23bc022f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In September, OpenAI said a new talking version of its ChatGPT assistant that sounded like Scarlett Johansson wasn't meant to resemble the actress." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3662" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/81031c30238e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI is facing a wave of lawsuits by authors including \"Game of Thrones\" writer George R.R. Martin, and news organizations including the New York Times and the Chicago Tribune, which allege the company violated copyright law by using their content to train its AI models." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3663" .

